{"kind":"request","text":"Current-basis replacement for notification regression #21312 (git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:903a86d6ce4e15ec6db2bd7b1e1d32d06f8a9853). This is distinct from oversized-attachment #20664, now successor #22093. The outcome, runtime constraints, performer and destination are unchanged. The original start-order condition was missed when #22092 mislabeled this task as20664; that does not discharge or replace the two earlier outcomes.\n\nRequester scheduling disposition: preserve the already-produced f1e108fc test-only candidate and its actual test evidence. Reconcile its reporting to this current request and obtain independent review when Codex has a safe checkpoint; do not discard useful source or rerun unchanged checks merely to relabel their execution. If rebinding requires a causal commit, preserve the identical tree, attribute carried gates to f1e108fc, and request review of the new exact head. In parallel with that review wait, begin the actual oversized-attachment assessment #22093 after your active21944 review; then preserve #20819 before further later implementations. This is an explicit disposition of incurred work, not a claim that the earlier queue was followed. No source implementation approval is given.\n\nClaude: add mounted regression coverage for the current notification read position, with the explicit scheduling reconciliation below. This is a small test-only follow-up from the closed-task audit; preserve active work and independent review turns.\n\nThe current [notification component](ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx@d70d8fe6a160a470a75cf613f0075b7695ef5c08:56), [storage helper](ui/src/lib/memory.ts@d70d8fe6a160a470a75cf613f0075b7695ef5c08:16), and [notification tests](ui/test/notifications.test.mjs@d70d8fe6a160a470a75cf613f0075b7695ef5c08:78) are byte-identical to current main d70d8fe6. The five tests clear storage before mounting, exercise in-memory interactions and never verify stored content or reload it. Each separate omission of load, save, actor key or room key leaves those five tests green. The attached independent mounted probe passes unchanged current source and fails for each omission. [Evidence](notification-storage-evidence.json), [probe addition](notification-storage-probe.mjs), and [four isolated mutations](notification-storage-mutations.diff) make the finding reproducible. This establishes a focused coverage gap, not a current runtime defect or a claim that every other UI test survives those mutations.\n\nThe older #1312 follow/read-watermark test was removed when adopted UI simplification c26a7f57/25981e55 removed that feature. Do not revive the old WorkDrawer, follow controls or personal filters. Protect the notification behavior that exists now. This is a separate outcome from batch recovery #21305, not a reason to expand or delay its commitment.","body":{"branch":"request/notification-storage-regression","conditions":"On a new request/notification-storage-regression worktree from then-current main, add the smallest mounted regression using the existing jsdom/React/Vite stack and actual localStorage path. Independently preseed a current identity read position; mount and verify the correct unread rows; mark a row or all read and check persisted content; remount and verify the saved result; switch room and actor and establish independent positions without overwriting the original. Keep existing notification navigation and out-of-order-read controls. Prefer independently specified storage expectations and observable rendered effects over mirroring helper output; no test-only component props or storage bypass. Prove each of four separate working omissions (mount load, event save, actor scoping, room scoping) is caught at the intended boundary, distinguishing runtime assertion failures from syntax/build errors. The attached probe is a starting point, not required implementation. Recheck current existing coverage before adding duplication. Test-only scope: no runtime semantics, new dependency, notification feature, restored old personal-work UI or workflow-state change. If a real runtime defect is found, report and assign that separate outcome before changing behavior. Acknowledge the current author refresh and the explicit scheduling disposition above; preserve all source and historical provenance. If relevant conditions or source change again before a later start, reconcile that change with the author. Run focused notification tests, full UI suite, TypeScript checks and applicable embed gate; record whether any generated bytes change. Publish a concise exact-head artifact with evidence/previews, request independent Codex Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the verdict, seal the approved head with exact-path succession, push main/workroom/receipt refs, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch. A test-only head preserves the runtime architecture contract; no forced architecture prose edit. No live reader operation, history rewrite, actor/key change, public publication or #8162 work.","head":"d70d8fe6a160a470a75cf613f0075b7695ef5c08","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2b37ee0d6ca43aca851fa186221aa23e5475a842, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bae33e6e9ff9f1d2e138724c5f52763383b7132d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c26a7f5736902f8679a47c1dd4434f3e59c2d011 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b8a9ff517318daec88e265b848e08ea877e98fa, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2ae9967b90652f1eee1b7d721c15dab99596e88f and 35 more","target_head":"d70d8fe6a160a470a75cf613f0075b7695ef5c08","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622